yu of the Southern Xiongnu in the late Eastern Han. Yufuluo, son of Chanyu Qiangqu, aided the Han in suppressing the rebellion of Zhang Chun, stranded in the Central Plains due to internal strife, he clashed with warlords like Yuan Shao and Cao Cao before eventually submitting to Cao Cao. His younger brother Huchuquan succeeded him and was detained upon visiting the imperial court. Yufuluo's son Liu Bao became the Left Worthy Prince, and his grandson Liu Yuan founded the state of Han-Zhao."},"talent":{"military":"9","commerce":"6","politics":"7"}}],"friendGroups":[],"body":null,"honorifics":[],"selfAddress":[],"specialNames":[],"vip":{"isVIP":0,"from":"0","to":"0"},"marriage":{"aiMarriageAge":"25","startPregnantAge":"0"},"scenarios":[{"story":{"id":"S10802","name":{"zh":"黄巾起义","en":"Yellow Turban Rebellion"},"year":"184","month":"3"},"faction":null,"city":"CS1033","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"2","role":0,"stats":[74,65,24,35,67,68],"title":-1,"rank":"9","loyalty":"0","reputation":"0","equipment":{"weapon":"WP1004902","armor":"WP1005805","helmet":"WP1023905","horse":"WP29009"},"couple":[]},{"story":{"id":"S10215","name":{"zh":"汉末三杰","en":"Three Heroes of the Late Han"},"year":"185","month":"3"},"faction":"WJ10172","city":"CS1075","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"2","role":1,"stats":[74,65,24,35,67,68],"title":1,"rank":"1","loyalty":"100","reputation":"0","equipment":{"weapon":"WP1004902","armor":"WP1005805","helmet":"WP1023905","horse":"WP29009"},"couple":[]},{"story":{"id":"S10615","name":{"zh":"十常侍之乱","en":"Turmoil of the Ten Attendants"},"year":"188","month":"11"},"faction":"WJ10147","city":"CS1015","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"2","role":0,"stats":[74,65,24,35,67,68],"title":-1,"rank":"9","loyalty":"90","reputation":"0","equipment":{"weapon":"WP1004902","armor":"WP1005805","helmet":"WP1023905","horse":"WP29009"},"couple":[]},{"story":{"id":"S10402","name":{"zh":"诸侯讨董","en":"Coalition Against Dong Zhuo"},"year":"190","month":"3"},"fa